# rpmlint overrides for the scoot RPMs, used by the openSUSE job in
# .github/workflows/rpm.yml (`rpmlint -r`). Fedora's job does not use
# this file: its dictionary passes the same lines, and an unused filter
# would itself fail there.
#
# 'config' is the standard term for config files and their ~/.config
# paths; openSUSE's en_US dictionary flags the bare token (Fedora's
# does not). Scoped to the exact token so a real typo still fails.

addFilter(r"spelling-error \('config',")
